{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268448,"nonce":"HRgNxx2SSSWYDXfZfWCB3exAGOo=","title":"ashui owns the icon system: a public icon macro, an icon element and a Remix catalogue package","message":"**What**\n\nChimpMonk (git-bug in that repo) and RayDE (bb19773 there) should share one icon system, and the user decided it belongs to ashui. ChimpMonk has it today in its editor package; this moves it.\n\n**Parts**\n\n- ashui.svg.IconSet, in core: `@:build(IconSet.build([dir, dir]))` compiles every SVG under the directories into a typed, lazily built `public static var NAME(get, never):SvgDocument` through SvgDocument.compileXml at compile time. Files are module dependencies, a name collision is a compile error, and the class is @:dce so only referenced icons reach a program. Several directories make one class. From ChimpMonk's editor/macros/SvgIcons.hx.\n- `\u003cicon document={...}/\u003e` in ashui-components: draws a compiled document through Svg, tinted by currentColor so text-* classes colour it. From ChimpMonk's editor/ui/Icon.hx.\n- A new haxelib, ashui-icons: ashui.icons.Remix, the Remix Icon set (3229 SVGs in 20 category folders, Apache-2.0, its licence carried) on the package's class path, so an app can also name it as \"ashui/icons/remix\" in its own IconSet.build to combine it with its own icons. ChimpMonk's three custom 3D icons (3d-move, 3d-rotate, 3d-scale) stay in ChimpMonk.\n- Maintainer notes, from ChimpMonk's docs/editor/maintaining/icons.md, written for ashui.\n\n**Decided**\n\nA separate package, so ashui itself does not carry 13 MB of SVG; chosen by the user over putting it in core.\n\n**Wiring**\n\nscripts/package_haxelib.py, the CI, publish and release workflows, docs/releases.md, the package fixtures and the README table list the packages; ashui-icons joins each.","files":null}]}